  "provider_lifecycle_findings": [
    "ReceiptWitness defines __enter__ and close, but no __exit__; the old with ReceiptWitness(...) expression fails before entering the provider.",
    "The actual __enter__ reads the original worker and writer callables, installs bounded observation patches through an ExitStack, returns self, and catches BaseException around partial installation to call its existing close before re-raising.",
    "The directory-sync availability refusal occurs before any patch installation; explicit entry does not introduce a new partial-cleanup path.",
    "closing receives the exact object returned by the actual ReceiptWitness.__enter__, returns that same object from its own entry, and invokes that object's close on normal or exceptional body exit.",
    "CPython's closing.__exit__ neither catches nor suppresses exceptions. A provider close exception propagates with its existing object identity and existing precedence over an active body exception; no original-failure preservation beyond current provider semantics is claimed.",
    "The inner WorkspaceRequestObserver context, including its real __exit__, runs first during unwinding, before the outer ReceiptWitness.close. All inner assertions, manual close calls, deliberate later-owner restoration, timeout limits, and native/HTTP call identity controls remain byte-exact outside the specified outer expression edits.",
    "Workspace PublicationObserver source is unchanged; this repair neither adds a provider compatibility shim nor changes public runtime behavior."
  ],
